<section class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">Support</h1>
  <p class="text-neutral-400 mb-12">
    Answers to the things people most often get stuck on. If yours isn't
    here, <%= link_to "get in touch", contact_path, class: "underline hover:text-neutral-300" %>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500 mb-4">For bands</h2>
  <div class="mb-12">
    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>I created my band but it doesn't show up publicly</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Every new band starts as <span class="text-white">pending</span> and is
          reviewed by the SceneCore team before it appears in
          <%= link_to "Bands", discover_bands_path, class: "underline hover:text-white" %>
          or at its public address.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can keep working while you wait — add albums, write posts, add
          members. It all goes live the moment your band is approved.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>I published something but nobody can see it</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Albums and posts are each <span class="text-white">draft</span> until
          you publish them, so a new album stays private until you say
          otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a whole page is invisible, check the band itself is approved — an
          unapproved band hides everything under it, however you set each item.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>How do I add my albums?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          From your band's page, search Spotify by album name and pick yours from
          the results. The title and cover come across automatically, and the
          album links straight back to Spotify for listening.
        </p>
        <p>
          Imported albums arrive as drafts, so you choose when they go live.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>Can I upload my audio files?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          No — and that's deliberate. SceneCore doesn't host audio. Your music
          plays through Spotify, so you keep your streams, your numbers and your
          existing distribution exactly as they are.
        </p>
        <p>
          SceneCore is where the relationship with your fans lives: your page,
          your posts, your followers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>The album cover is missing or broken</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Spotify's image links expire, so an album imported a while ago can lose
          its cover. Open the album and use
          <span class="text-white">Refetch from Spotify</span> to read it again.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also point at an image URL of your own, and that one takes
          precedence from then on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>Who can see each post?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          A published post is either <span class="text-white">public</span>, visible
          to anyone, or <span class="text-white">followers</span>, visible only to
          people who follow your band. Someone who unfollows loses access to the
          follower posts straight away.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>How do I add someone to my band?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Band administrators can add members from the band's Members page. The
          person needs a SceneCore account first — you pick them from the list of
          existing users, so ask them to sign up before you go looking for them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Members can manage the band's content. Administrators can do that and
          also edit the band and manage members.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>I can't remove or demote an administrator</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          A band can never be left without an administrator, so the last one can't
          be removed or turned into a member. Promote someone else to
          administrator first, then make the change.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500 mb-4">For fans</h2>
  <div class="mb-12">
    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>How do I follow a band?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Open the band's page and use Follow — you'll need an account. Following
          unlocks that band's follower-only posts, and you can unfollow from the
          same place at any time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>A band I'm looking for isn't here</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Only approved bands appear in search and in
          <%= link_to "Bands", discover_bands_path, class: "underline hover:text-white" %>.
          If a band hasn't joined SceneCore yet, the band itself has to create its
          page — we don't create pages on a band's behalf.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>Where does the music actually play?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          On Spotify, embedded in the band's page. Playback follows your own
          Spotify account and its usual rules, so plays count for the band the
          same way they always have.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500 mb-4">Your account</h2>
  <div class="mb-12">
    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>I forgot my password</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          Use
          <%= link_to "Forgot your password?", new_user_password_path, class: "underline hover:text-white" %>
          on the sign-in page and we'll email you a reset link. Check your spam
          folder if it doesn't arrive.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group border-b border-neutral-800 py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-white marker:hidden flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <span>How do I change my name or email?</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="text-neutral-300 mt-3 space-y-2">
        <p>
          From your profile. One account can follow bands and belong to bands at
          the same time — there's no need for a separate account to be a fan of
          someone else's band.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/40 p-6">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Still stuck?</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 mb-5">
      Tell us what happened and what you expected — it gets us to an answer much
      faster.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Contact us", contact_path, class: "rounded-full bg-yellow-400/10 text-yellow-300 border border-yellow-500/30 font-semibold px-6 py-3 hover:bg-yellow-400/20 hover:text-yellow-200 transition" %>
      <%= link_to "How it works", how_it_works_path, class: "rounded-full border border-neutral-700 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 hover:border-neutral-500 transition" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
